WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.929
- We're back with Sterling K. Brown.

00:00:02.929 --> 00:00:05.060
(audience cheering and clapping)

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:06.250
His show, "This Is Us"

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.780
is back on NBC starting January 4th.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.320
So, let's talk "This Is Us".

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.520
Like, how are you feeling?
Is it bittersweet?

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.380
Because this is such a brilliant cast.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.970
The chemistry has done so well.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.150
It's such a popular show.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:20.770
And it's just such a great message

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:22.100
to the family vibe from the show,

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.340
which has been so great overall.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.278
So, is it kind of bittersweet for you?

00:00:25.278 --> 00:00:26.111
Are you excited to do other things,

00:00:26.111 --> 00:00:27.420
but you're also like kinda sad?

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.180
- That's exactly what it is.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.080
I love the show.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:30.913
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:30.913 --> 00:00:32.130
- It's been one of the best

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.190
six year ride of my life.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:35.023
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:35.023 --> 00:00:35.856
- Like professionally,

00:00:35.856 --> 00:00:36.689
it's been absolutely amazing.

00:00:36.689 --> 00:00:37.960
Beautiful people.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.606
I'm looking at my Black
Pearson family over here,

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:42.190
and I've gotten a chance

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:43.470
to see these three little girls

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:44.542
grow up over time.

00:00:44.542 --> 00:00:46.740
Like every time I'm on
stage with them, alright,

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:47.840
I'm, I'm gonna miss them.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.670
And I see their parents who
were backstage with them,

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:51.102
and I was like, "I love your daughters."

00:00:51.102 --> 00:00:51.935
- And you've watched them grow up.

00:00:51.935 --> 00:00:53.770
- And I've literally watched them grow up.

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:56.150
So once we start to get to like the last

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.010
two or three episodes,

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:59.720
there'll be something that happens

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.610
that I won't be able
to stop from happening.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:02.713
- Oh, no.

00:01:02.713 --> 00:01:03.950
- Because I know I'm
actually saying goodbye.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:04.783
- Right now, I'm like "Oh, we're

00:01:04.783 --> 00:01:06.890
having a great time" and
just blah, blah, blah.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:08.020
When it gets to the end,

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:08.853
- [Kelly] Oh no.

00:01:08.853 --> 00:01:09.686
- there'll be no acting.

00:01:09.686 --> 00:01:10.519
- It'll be ugly cry.

00:01:10.519 --> 00:01:11.573
- It'll be ugly.

